Expand Up  |  @@ -151,6 +151,25 @@ Bug Fixes since HDF5-1.13.3 release   
<::before> |  <::before> |  <::before>===================================   
<::before> |  <::before> |  <::before> Library   
<::before> |  <::before> |  <::before> \-------   
|  <::before> |  <::before> \- Fixed a heap buffer overflow that occurs when reading from   
|  <::before> |  <::before> a dataset with a compact layout within a malformed HDF5 file   
|  <::before> |  <::before>   
  
|  <::before> |  <::before> During opening of a dataset that has a compact layout, the   
|  <::before> |  <::before> library allocates a buffer that stores the dataset's raw data.   
|  <::before> |  <::before> The dataset's object header that gets written to the file   
|  <::before> |  <::before> contains information about how large of a buffer the library   
|  <::before> |  <::before> should allocate. If this object header is malformed such that   
|  <::before> |  <::before> it causes the library to allocate a buffer that is too small   
|  <::before> |  <::before> to hold the dataset's raw data, future I/O to the dataset can   
|  <::before> |  <::before> result in heap buffer overflows. To fix this issue, an extra   
|  <::before> |  <::before> check is now performed for compact datasets to ensure that   
|  <::before> |  <::before> the size of the allocated buffer matches the expected size   
|  <::before> |  <::before> of the dataset's raw data (as calculated from the dataset's   
|  <::before> |  <::before> dataspace and datatype information). If the two sizes do not   
|  <::before> |  <::before> match, opening of the dataset will fail.   
|  <::before> |  <::before>   
  
|  <::before> |  <::before> (JTH - 2023/04/04, GH-2606)   
|  <::before> |  <::before>   
  
<::before> |  <::before> |  <::before> \- Fixed a memory corruption issue that can occur when reading   
<::before> |  <::before> |  <::before> from a dataset using a hyperslab selection in the file   
<::before> |  <::before> |  <::before> dataspace and a point selection in the memory dataspace   
